      "text": "## The Big Picture: A Neoplasm Is a Clone That Escaped the Controls on Cell Number"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-NEOPLASIA-CARCINOGENESIS-AND-TUMOR-BIOLOGY.md#007",
      "path": [
        "05-NEOPLASIA-CARCINOGENESIS-AND-TUMOR-BIOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:pathology:05-neoplasia-carcinogenesis-and-tumor-biology]",
        "canonical_path": "pathology/05-NEOPLASIA-CARCINOGENESIS-AND-TUMOR-BIOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[neoplasia-autonomy, differentiation-anaplasia, nomenclature-principles, hallmarks-of-cancer, carcinogenesis, invasion-metastasis]",
        "current_path": "pathology/05-NEOPLASIA-CARCINOGENESIS-AND-TUMOR-BIOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:pathology:neoplasia-carcinogenesis-and-tumor-biology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "pathology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[neoplasia]",
        "section": "pathology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Neoplasia, Carcinogenesis, and Tumor Biology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The novice mental model is \"cancer = fast-growing cells.\" The expert model is that a neoplasm\nis a **clone of cells that has acquired autonomy from the controls that normally regulate cell\nnumber** — it grows in a **heritable, self-directed** way that *persists after the initiating\nstimulus is gone*, which is exactly what separates it from the adaptations of `01`\n(hyperplasia stops when its driver stops; a neoplasm does not). Cancer is therefore best\nunderstood as **somatic evolution**: a population of cells accumulating heritable changes,\nunder selection, escaping one growth control after another."
    },
    {
      "id": "05-NEOPLASIA-CARCINOGENESIS-AND-TUMOR-BIOLOGY.md#008",
      "path": [
        "05-NEOPLASIA-CARCINOGENESIS-AND-TUMOR-BIOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
